{"repositoryId":1415821668,"availability":"available","full":"joakimeriksson/fm1-emu","name":"fm1-emu","description":"Emulator for the M-VAVE FM-1 pocket synth: runs its firmwares unchanged in the browser and natively","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":53,"forks":15,"created":"2026-10-12T15:57:42Z","updated":"2026-10-19T13:08:04Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://joakimeriksson.github.io/fm1-emu/","topics":["c64","chiptune","emulator","fm-1","fm-synthesis","jit","m-vave","midi","reverse-engineering","rust","sid","synthesizer","web-audio","webassembly"],"demo":"https://joakimeriksson.github.io/fm1-emu/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:46.243Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:46.243Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:46.243Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T18:05:46.243Z","stars":53,"forks":15}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The M-VAVE FM-1 is a pocket FM synthesizer, and a small community writes its own firmwares for it: drum machines, grooveboxes, ambient generators, a chord harp. This project emulates the FM-1 itself, its CPU, screen, keys, knobs and audio, so every one of those firmwares runs unchanged in a browser, on a computer or as an instrument plugin in a DAW (AU, VST3). You can try a firmware before you install it, write one without a synth on the desk, or just play.","Play it: joakimeriksson.github.io/fm1-emu: pick a firmware, press Start, play with the computer keyboard, the mouse, a touch screen or a MIDI keyboard.","With sound: nine of the firmwares in 50 seconds."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/joakimeriksson/fm1-emu/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"d76077bf535089f044079ed0b7a6a814368d28e6b7a6893b7e4bf624a5c46232","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:46.304Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T18:05:46.304Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The M-VAVE FM-1 is a pocket FM synthesizer, and a small commun